{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnustomeleecombat"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"The-bundle","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat","doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/init(text:)","doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/verbs","doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/actions"],"title":"The bundle"},{"anchor":"Registering-a-villain","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/villain(_:key:strength:weapons:prose:onDefeat:)","doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/aggression(of:key:daemonName:strikesFirst:playerStrength:while:prose:)"],"title":"Registering a villain"},{"anchor":"Traits-the-host-declares-on-its-items","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/Gnusto\/TraitKey\/weapon","doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/Gnusto\/TraitKey\/weaponStrength"],"title":"Traits the host declares on its items"},{"anchor":"The-systems-own-voice","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/CombatText","doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/CombatText\/init()","doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/CombatText\/attackFutile","doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/CombatText\/noWeapon","doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/CombatText\/notAWeapon","doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/CombatText\/weaponNotHeld"],"title":"The system’s own voice"},{"anchor":"A-villains-lines","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/VillainProse","doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/VillainProse\/init(miss:wound:knockout:death:)","doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/VillainProse\/miss","doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/VillainProse\/wound","doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/VillainProse\/knockout","doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/VillainProse\/death"],"title":"A villain’s lines"},{"anchor":"His-counter-attack-lines","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/AggressionProse","doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/AggressionProse\/init(miss:wound:playerDeath:)","doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/AggressionProse\/miss","doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/AggressionProse\/wound","doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/AggressionProse\/playerDeath"],"title":"His counter-attack lines"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The engine ships "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"attack"},{"type":"text","text":" as a stub verb, so every game already knows the word"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and answers it with a sentence. This library takes the word over and puts a body"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"behind it. A swing resolves a weapon, rolls once out of a hundred against a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per-weapon table, and spends the villain’s health; a knockout puts him on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"floor for 2 turns; the last hit prints his death line, runs the host’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onDefeat"},{"type":"text","text":" hook, and removes him from play. The exchange a player recognizes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from Zork — swing, answer, swing — is written nowhere. It falls out of the turn"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pipeline: the player’s blow resolves in the command stages and the villain’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lands with the end-of-turn timers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Because the library claims ","type":"text"},{"code":".attack","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"MeleeCombat(text:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is where that verb’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"voice lives. ","type":"text"},{"code":"text.stubs.attack","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the line a game without combat","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"prints, and a game with this library never prints it. The four refusals the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mechanics own — swinging at something no villain rule claimed, swinging","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bare-handed, naming a feather as a weapon, naming a sword you aren’t holding —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/CombatText","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", passed at init.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"GameContent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" bundle rather than a ","type":"text"},{"code":"GamePlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" because it saves a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ledger: each villain’s health, his stun countdown, whether he is currently in a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fight, and the player’s own wounds, keyed by a string the host chooses. Nothing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"else belongs to it. The villains are the host’s actors, the weapons are the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"host’s items carrying the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/Gnusto\/TraitKey\/weapon"},{"type":"text","text":" trait, and every line"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"either side speaks arrives as "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/VillainProse","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/AggressionProse","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which carry no defaults at all — a library"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cannot guess a villain’s death sentence."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every roll draws from the game’s seeded stream, so a pinned seed replays a fight"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"blow for blow. The guards are ordered so quiet turns draw nothing: a villain in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"another room, or behind a closed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"while:"},{"type":"text","text":" gate, or already engaged, burns no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"randomness, which is what keeps one villain’s presence from shifting another"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"villain’s draws. Two simplifications are deliberate and want ledgering per game:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the player’s wounds never heal, and a defeated villain stays defeated."}]},{"anchor":"Wiring-it-in","text":"Wiring it in","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mark the weapons, register each villain in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rules"},{"type":"text","text":", and splice his"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"counter-attack daemon into "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timers"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Gnusto","import GnustoMeleeCombat","","struct Cavern: Game {","    let melee = MeleeCombat()","","    let sword = Item {","        name(\"elvish sword\")","        trait(.weapon, true)","        trait(.weaponStrength, 3)   \/\/ a keen blade: misses less, kills more","    }","    let troll = Actor { name(\"troll\") }","    let axe = Item { name(\"bloody axe\") }","    @Global var passageClear = false","","    var content: GameContents { melee }","","    var rules: Rules {","        melee.villain(","            troll, key: \"troll\", strength: 2,","            weapons: [sword],","            prose: MeleeCombat.VillainProse(","                miss: [\"The troll swings; the axe bites air.\"],","                wound: [\"Your blow lands, and the troll grunts.\"],","                knockout: \"The troll drops where he stood, out cold.\",","                death: \"The troll dies, and his body dissolves.\"),","            onDefeat: {","                passageClear = true          \/\/ unbar the door","                axe.move(to: player.location)  \/\/ and drop the loot","            })","    }","","    var timers: [TimedEvent] {","        melee.aggression(","            of: troll, key: \"troll\", daemonName: \"melee.troll\",","            strikesFirst: 33,","            prose: MeleeCombat.AggressionProse(","                miss: [\"The axe passes within an inch of your ear.\"],","                wound: [\"The axe catches your shoulder.\"],","                playerDeath: \"The troll's axe removes your head.\"))","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The two calls share a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"key:"},{"type":"text","text":", and that is the whole of the connection between"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them. A villain registered with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"villain"},{"type":"text","text":" alone never fights back and stays down"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for good once knocked out; one given an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"aggression"},{"type":"text","text":" daemon wakes up on his own."}]},{"text":"The numbers","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"The-numbers"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/Gnusto\/TraitKey\/weaponStrength","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" slides the outcome cutpoints, out of 100.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Strength 2 is the baseline — miss ≤ 30, wound ≤ 70, knockout ≤ 85, kill above —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so a plain ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/Gnusto\/TraitKey\/weapon","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" with no keenness declared fights as it did","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"before the trait existed. Strength 1 or less is a clumsy blade at 40\/76\/90;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"3 or more is a keen one at 22\/64\/82. When the player names no weapon, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keenest one he is holding serves.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The counter-attack rolls a flat table: miss ≤ 50, wound ≤ 85, an outright kill","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"above. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"playerStrength"},{"text":" is how many wounds the player survives, default 2.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"strikesFirst"},{"text":" is the odds out of 100 that a villain starts a fight on a turn","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the player hasn’t — 100 fights on sight, 0 only ever answers a blow, and neither","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of those two values draws from the stream. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"while:"},{"type":"text","text":" is an extra gate checked"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before the same-room guard, for a villain whose combat is scoped to one room; it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"does not gate coming round from a knockout, so a man knocked out where his gate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is shut still wakes up."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"The-worked-example","text":"The worked example"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sources\/Zork1\/"},{"type":"text","text":" wires two villains against this library. The troll is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"straightforward one: he blocks a passage, starts a fight one turn in three, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"his axe is lootable once he falls. The thief is the awkward one, and is why"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"while:"},{"type":"text","text":" exists — he prowls the whole underground picking pockets and fights"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only in his own lair, so his gate is closed on almost every turn he is alive."}]}]}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"GnustoMeleeCombat"}],"externalID":"GnustoMeleeCombat","title":"GnustoMeleeCombat","role":"collection","roleHeading":"Framework"},"abstract":[{"text":"The attack verbs promoted to a mechanic: weapons, villain health, and a villain who answers.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"references":{"doc://GnustoMeleeCombat/documentation/GnustoMeleeCombat/MeleeCombat/AggressionProse/playerDeath":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Handed to "},{"code":"die(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when the last hit lands."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat\/AggressionProse\/playerDeath","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnustomeleecombat\/meleecombat\/aggressionprose\/playerdeath","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"playerDeath"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"playerDeath"},"doc://GnustoMeleeCombat/documentation/GnustoMeleeCombat/MeleeCombat":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"MeleeCombat","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MeleeCombat"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MeleeCombat"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/documentation\/GnustoMeleeCombat\/MeleeCombat","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Zork-style-lite melee: the engine’s attack verbs promoted to real behavior,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a weapon trait, per-villain health, a seeded outcome table (miss \/ wound \/","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"knockout \/ kill), and an aggression daemon so villains hit back.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Deterministic under a pinned seed — every roll draws from the game’s saved"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"random stream."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnustomeleecombat\/meleecombat"},"doc://GnustoMeleeCombat/documentation/GnustoMeleeCombat":{"title":"GnustoMeleeCombat","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The attack verbs promoted to a mechanic: weapons, villain health, and a villain who answers."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnustomeleecombat","k